          <circle class="dot" cx="1010" cy="90" r="10"/><text class="st" x="1010" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Review</text><text class="sub" x="1010" y="147" text-anchor="middle">claims against the diff</text>
        </svg>
        <ol class="words" id="evidence-words">
          <li><b>Implement</b><small class="k">.agents/completion/&lt;issue&gt;.json</small><p class="cond">Per acceptance criterion: met or not, and what shows it.</p></li>
          <li><b>Verify</b><small class="k">verify.sh</small><p class="cond">Every check of verify.conf; the pass is bound to the content fingerprint.</p></li>
          <li><b>Completion gate</b><small class="k">complete | awaiting_evidence</small><p class="cond">Partial: the implementer is started again.</p></li>
          <li class="ask"><b>You answer</b><small>blocked</small><p class="cond">The run stops with the question.</p></li>
          <li><b>Review</b><small>each claimed criterion against the diff</small></li>
        </ol>
      </figure>
      <pre role="region" class="excerpt" aria-label="Excerpt of the description of pull request 249"><span class="src">{bare(pull(249))} · excerpt</span>Completion: complete
- met: Every statement links to or matches its source; no invented figure or testimonial. (website/src/pages/{"{"}features,examples,about{"}"}.astro: each feature section names its file and key with repoFile links and the PRs that built it; [...])
[...]
- met: ./scripts/verify.sh passes. (./scripts/verify.sh run as the last step of the session; result in the final message.)

Verification:
- ./scripts/verify.sh passed</pre>
      <Table>
        <caption>The statuses of the completion record <code>.agents/completion/&lt;issue&gt;.json</code> and what the scripts do with them, from <code>.agents/prompts/implementer.md</code>.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">status</th><th scope="col">meaning</th><th scope="col">next</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="k">complete</th><td data-col="meaning">Every criterion met or not applicable, nothing remains</td><td data-col="next">review, commit, pull request</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="k">awaiting_evidence</th><td data-col="meaning">Everything that can be shown now is shown; a criterion waits for CI, your approval or the merge</td><td data-col="next">pull request; the Issue closes when the evidence exists</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="k">partial</th><td data-col="meaning">Work remains, whatever the reason</td><td data-col="next">the implementer is started again</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="k">blocked</th><td data-col="meaning">A decision only you can make</td><td data-col="next">the run stops with the question</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </Table>
      <p><code>verify.sh</code> runs every check of <code>scripts/verify.conf</code>, and its pass is bound to a content fingerprint and reused while nothing changes. Every commit needs the full verification; a partial run of some groups, which a repair round may use, is never a verification and cannot be cited. The reviewer holds each claimed criterion against the diff, and an unsupported claim comes back as a finding.</p>
